{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## F18 implementation kickoff\n\nResolved F18 as `immolated-holohedral-waterdogs` with canonical ID `a9ec-37db-0d91-483b`. The isolated worktree is `/Users/joeoakhart/f18-user-guide-20260823` at `origin/main` commit `ae4030bd4a920762e27971f59a7aafdc4fcc0026`. The only permitted file is `docs/user-guide.md`.\n\nThe first plan-review attempt reproduced the concurrent ref-fetch error tracked by `agrologic-oval-bobolink`. The complete error and a successful serialized control were recorded on that bug. The second review produced a signed PASS with one P6 advisory. The advisory is deferred because D1 and D2 independently verify both named checks. F18 is claimed without an explicit assignee.\n\nThe implementation will add the client meaning of `caused_by` and replace selected router, blame-selection, credential-incident, and session-pointer internals with supported client behavior. The full suite is excluded because the change is Markdown-only. Focused contracts, documentation checks, lint, typecheck, and diff checks remain required."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787528573299449001,"uuid":"29c12fc7-b71d-4e63-b93c-1a10c9d3570d"}